# A2A payment safety

- Read `docs/BEGINNER_SETUP.md`, `docs/TESTNET_RUNBOOK.md`, and the nearest `AGENTS.md`.
- Read installed Next.js docs before changing route or proxy conventions.
- Keep demo, testnet, and mainnet as separate trust domains.
- Give the LLM a URL-only tool. Deterministic code owns payer binding, merchant, canonical token,
  amount, task budget, network, validity window, nonce, and idempotency.
- Use CAIP-2 network IDs. Never trust a token symbol or transaction hash by itself.
- Synthetic receipts/signatures may unlock only `/api/clearing/demo/*`.
- Testnet/mainnet settlement requires PostgreSQL and official facilitator verification.
- Never read, print, request, generate, or commit wallet/API secrets.
- Keep `CLEARING_MAINNET_ENABLED=false` during A-stage work.
- If infrastructure is missing, preserve the 503 fail-closed behavior.
